<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Cloud Cap Inn by the Tilly Jane Ski Trail, down the Cloud Cap road</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:209-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.414500" lon="-121.602200"><ele>1161.3</ele><name>Nordic skiers' sno-park (Tilly Jane Sno-Park)</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:cooper-spur-sno-park (OSM way 551745125); confidence: high; pdf_page: 210; book_elev_ft: 3800; quote: map 43: NORDIC SKIER PARKING 3800'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.414464" lon="-121.603366"><ele>1164.9</ele><name>Steep connector trail leaves the Cloud Cap road</name><desc>source: OSM node 4123263270, end of Tilly Jane Ski Trail #643 (way 410504468) on Cloud Cap Road; USFS SNO-643 BMP 0; owner's recording starts 10 m away; confidence: high; pdf_page: 212; quote: Just west of the small sno-park, on the left side of the Cloud Cap road, a 1-mile trail climbs steeply to join the main Tilly Jane Ski Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.409834" lon="-121.615908"><ele>1295.0</ele><name>Connector meets the Polallie Ridge trail (the ski route goes up the crest, 643A)</name><desc>source: OSM node 4123263229 on Tilly Jane Ski Trail #643, start of Polallie Ridge Trail #643A (way 5041080); 0.89 mi from wp 2 on the owner's recording; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 212; quote: a 1-mile trail climbs steeply to join the main Tilly Jane Ski Trail ... Once on the ridgetop, ski the wide, easy-to-follow trail upward to the Tilly Jane Campground</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.399093" lon="-121.647021"><ele>1745.1</ele><name>Tilly Jane cabins (A-frame)</name><desc>source: OSM node 4229908294, upper end of Tilly Jane Ski Trail #643 (way 410504468) at Tilly Jane Campground (node 1616078109, 40 m W); A-frame (way 722330441) 110 m E; 643A ends 40 m E; confidence: high; pdf_page: 212; book_elev_ft: 5720; quote: At 5,720 feet, 0.6 mile below Cloud Cap Inn, the trail levels out and passes directly in front of two cabins on the left</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.403179" lon="-121.651849"><ele>1740.9</ele><name>Roadbed meets the Cloud Cap road</name><desc>source: OSM node 33445305, Tilly Jane House Road NF 3512630 (way 5040850) x Cloud Cap Road NF 3512; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 212; quote: After leaving the cabins, you soon cross a small ravine ... From there follow a roadbed to the main Cloud Cap road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.404494" lon="-121.651692"><ele>1746.8</ele><name>Leave the road below the inn</name><desc>source: OSM Cloud Cap Road node 33426126, 172 m along the road from wp 6 where it bends right; confidence: low; pdf_page: 212; quote: follow the roadbed 200 yards to where it turns right. Leave the road here and climb left up a short, steep hillside to the inn</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.404050" lon="-121.654500"><ele>1801.4</ele><name>Cloud Cap Inn</name><desc>source: centroid of OSM building way 293136649 'Cloud Cap Inn' (ele tag 1793 m = 5883 ft); confidence: high; pdf_page: 210; book_elev_ft: 5920; quote: map 43: CLOUD CAP INN 5920'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.414500" lon="-121.602200"><ele>1161.3</ele><name>Back at the sno-park by the Cloud Cap road</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin; confidence: high; pdf_page: 212; quote: Most skiers descend to the trailhead by way of the Cloud Cap road, which offers a gentle grade all the way</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Cloud Cap Inn by the Tilly Jane Ski Trail, down the Cloud Cap road</name><desc>1. Nordic skiers' sno-park (Tilly Jane Sno-Park) -&gt; Steep connector trail leaves the Cloud Cap road: osm (high), 0.07 mi | 2. Steep connector trail leaves the Cloud Cap road -&gt; Connector meets the Polallie Ridge trail (the ski route goes up the crest, 643A): line (high), 0.72 mi | 3. Connector meets the Polallie Ridge trail (the ski route goes up the crest, 643A) -&gt; Tilly Jane cabins (A-frame): line (high), 2.71 mi | 4. Tilly Jane cabins (A-frame) -&gt; Roadbed meets the Cloud Cap road: usfs-road (medium), 0.51 mi | 5. Roadbed meets the Cloud Cap road -&gt; Leave the road below the inn: osm (medium), 0.11 mi | 6. Leave the road below the inn -&gt; Cloud Cap Inn: straight (medium), 0.14 mi | 7. Cloud Cap Inn -&gt; Back at the sno-park by the Cloud Cap road: osm (high), 8.84 mi</desc>
